# ColorTheory — app configuration
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in. Restart with `npx expo start --clear` after edits.
#
# EVERYTHING prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ IS EMBEDDED IN THE APP BUNDLE AND READABLE BY ANYONE.
# Only put values here that are designed to be public. Row Level Security protects the data.
#
# NEVER put these in this file (they belong in Supabase Edge Function secrets):
#   service-role / secret keys (sb_secret_…), ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, FASHN_API_KEY, CLEANUP_SECRET,
#   database passwords, signing keys.
# The app refuses to start its Supabase client if it detects a secret/service-role key here.

# ── Supabase (optional — without it the app runs in on-device/demo mode) ─────────────────────
# Project Settings → API. Use the *publishable* key (sb_publishable_…) on new projects…
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# …or the legacy anon JWT on older projects (used only if the publishable key is empty).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Providers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Colour analysis: device (default, private, offline) | remote (Edge Function + AI vision) | mock
EXPO_PUBLIC_ANALYSIS_PROVIDER=device
# Outfit previews: mock (default, labelled demo) | remote (Edge Function + FASHN try-on) | off
EXPO_PUBLIC_OUTFIT_GENERATION=mock

# ── Product ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Offer "Explore in demo mode" on the welcome screen. Defaults: on without Supabase or in
# development; off in production builds that have Supabase.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ENABLE_DEMO_MODE=
# Links to your published, reviewed legal documents (in-app summaries are shown otherwise).
EXPO_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_TERMS_URL=
